course: dictionary
lesson: 13111
title: Perfect with no faults
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are like a score of full marks. Flawless is one of them. It means perfect, with no mistakes, marks or faults at all. «Her dive into the pool was flawless.» You can picture it: she went in with no splash and no wobble.
explain: Look at the words around flawless to check. «The painting was flawless, with no smudges and no torn corners.» The clues are no smudges and no torn corners. Those are all faults, so flawless must mean that there are none. Try the swap: "The painting had no faults" fits, so you have it right.
explain: People also use flawless to praise something. «The actor gave a flawless performance.» That does not mean the actor was perfect as a person. It means the performance had no mistakes, so it was excellent. Flawless is high praise.
fact: Flawless means perfect, without any mistakes, marks or faults.
fact: «Flawless skin» means skin with no spots, marks or blemishes.
fact: «Almost flawless» means nearly perfect, with only a tiny fault.
fact: A flawless dive is one with no splash and no mistakes in the movements.
fact: You can use flawless about things you can see, like a diamond, or about things you do, like a performance.
exercise: «Her dive into the pool was flawless, with no splash at all.» What does flawless mean here? | Very loud | Slow and tired | Wet and cold | *Perfect, with no mistakes
exercise: «The cake was flawless, with no cracks and no burnt spots.» Find and copy one word that means perfect. | cake | spots | *flawless | burnt
exercise: Tom's drawing had no smudges or mistakes. Which word fits best? Tom's drawing was ___. | barely | glum | ancient | *flawless
test: «Almost flawless» means nearly perfect, with only a tiny fault. What does almost flawless mean? | *Nearly perfect, with only a tiny fault | Totally broken | Very old | Very hungry
test: The reviewer wrote, «a flawless performance». What does the reviewer think? | The actor was too quiet to hear | The actor forgot every line | *The actor made no mistakes at all | The actor was on stage for a short time
exam: Which phrase praises skin with no spots or marks? | Curt reply | Glum voice | Famished dog | *Flawless skin
